course: dictionary
lesson: 2315
title: Croquet and the mad game
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Croquet is a lawn game, so context can help you work out what it is. In «a game of croquet» the word game tells you it is something you play. In «the strangest croquet ever» the balls, mallets and arches are named, so you can picture the game.
explain: The clues are in the other words. «Live hedgehogs for balls, live flamingoes for mallets, and soldiers bent double for the arches» tells you that balls, mallets and arches are the parts of the game. Balls are round, mallets are sticks, and arches are the hoops that the ball must go through.
explain: Do not stop at the word you do not know. Read on, then check your idea by putting it back into the sentence. If «croquet» were a kind of dinner, would «the strangest croquet ever» still make sense with hedgehogs as balls? It would not, so croquet must be a game.
fact: Croquet is a lawn game played with wooden balls, long-handled wooden mallets and small metal hoops.
fact: Croquet is played in gardens and clubs, especially in the UK, Ireland, New Zealand and Australia, often in summer.
fact: «A croquet lawn» is the grass where the game is played.
fact: In Alice in Wonderland, the Queen's croquet game is mad: the balls are live hedgehogs and the hoops are soldiers bent over.
fact: As a verb, which is rare, «to croquet» means to knock another player's ball away by hitting your own ball against it.
exercise: «A croquet lawn is where players hit wooden balls with long-handled mallets.» Where is croquet played? | *On a grass lawn | In a bedroom | On a frozen lake | In a swimming pool
exercise: Normally, what is a croquet mallet made of? | Metal | Glass | *Wood | Plastic
exercise: «Its neck bends, so the flamingo keeps twisting round, and it would be a useless croquet mallet.» Why would the flamingo be useless as a mallet? | It has no feathers | It is too small to see | *Its neck bends, so it cannot hit the ball straight | It is too heavy to lift
test: «The hoops are soldiers bent over.» What are hoops in croquet? | Round wooden balls | *Small metal hoops stuck in the grass | Long wooden sticks | Little dogs
test: If you croquet another player's ball, what do you do? | *Hit your ball against theirs to knock it away | Hide their ball in your pocket | Count the hoops out loud | Throw your mallet over the hedge
exam: Which word means the long-handled wooden hammer used to hit the ball in croquet? | lawn | *mallet | hoop | arch
